  "meta": {
    "probe": "crass-collage-b",
    "target": "same target as crass-collage, inverted: a montage printed as a negative, white figures on a black field, with the type in the only other colour",
    "method": "inverting the plate turns the pack's fifteen vector outlines from bad photographs into good stencils. A silhouette that reads as a blob in black on white reads as a cut-out in white on black, because the eye stops asking it for detail. This is the only move in the whole test that improves what the fragment library can do without adding anything to it",
    "notDone": "still no photographic material and still no continuous tone. The hatch is engraving at a fixed spacing, and there is no gradient style, so nothing on this sheet has a value between the four in the palette"
  },
  "root": {
    "id": "root",
    "type": "group",
    "children": [
